<!--
  Google Material Symbols "edit_calendar" (outlined), shown beside a clicker
  card's date/time value on the edit screen; tapping it opens a normal picker to
  override the value.

  Bundled here rather than taken from androidx material-icons-extended: that
  library is generated from the older Material Icons set, which has no
  edit_calendar — the glyph exists only in Material Symbols.

  Traced verbatim from the Material Symbols source, whose viewBox is
  "0 -960 960 960"; a VectorDrawable viewport always starts at 0,0, so the
  group's translateY shifts the path down into it. Icon() tints it with the
  current content color, so the fillColor here is only a placeholder.
-->
